error[NK1370]: This `emit` in rule `line` could be undone: option 2 of a choice in rule `items` can still be tried after it runs.
   --> tests/grammar_emit_undone.nika:12:36
    |
 12 | 	rule line = w:until(";") ";" -> { emit Item { word: w.clone() } }
    |                                    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    |
    = note: The item goes to the caller's walk when the action runs (ADR-grammar-typed-read-v1 D7): if what follows the call of `line` fails, the parse goes back and tries option 2 of a choice in rule `items`, and the item is already handed over. The compiler does not hold items back to hide that.
    = help: Commit before the call: a cut `=>` in front of it, or the choice made before it, so that the parse cannot go back past the `emit`.
